1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,165
This video is a general guide to your second assignment, the data quality mini project around week eleven.

2
00:00:08,165 --> 00:00:13,325
Always follow your own assignment brief for the exact requirements.

3
00:00:13,325 --> 00:00:16,637
This guide shows how to apply module three:

4
00:00:16,637 --> 00:00:21,336
auditing, cleaning, imputing, treating outliers and encoding.

5
00:00:22,136 --> 00:00:28,897
The assignment is a formative mini project worth twenty five percent, mapped to outcome three:

6
00:00:28,897 --> 00:00:37,455
design and implement pre-processing and transformation strategies that improve data quality and analytical reliability.

7
00:00:37,455 --> 00:00:39,253
The key idea is evidence:

8
00:00:39,253 --> 00:00:44,288
show the problem, show your fix, and show the result before and after.

9
00:00:45,088 --> 00:00:48,240
Follow the module three pipeline.

10
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:49,672
Audit the data.

11
00:00:49,672 --> 00:00:52,920
Check the four quality dimensions.

12
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:56,740
Integrate sources and remove duplicates.

13
00:00:56,740 --> 00:01:01,993
Handle missing values and explain why they are missing.

14
00:01:01,993 --> 00:01:04,476
Detect and treat outliers.

15
00:01:04,476 --> 00:01:08,774
Encode categories and handle class imbalance.

16
00:01:08,774 --> 00:01:10,684
Validate with rules.

17
00:01:10,684 --> 00:01:12,976
And document every step.

18
00:01:13,776 --> 00:01:17,486
For every problem you find, record it in a log:

19
00:01:17,486 --> 00:01:23,407
what it is, how many rows, why you think it happened, and what you decided.

20
00:01:23,407 --> 00:01:26,881
Flag suspicious values before deleting them.

21
00:01:26,881 --> 00:01:34,854
Disguised missing values such as zero or nine ninety nine should be converted to real missing values.

22
00:01:34,854 --> 00:01:41,880
Re-run the audit after every fix, because standardising labels can create new duplicates.

23
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:48,222
When you fix missing values or outliers, compare before and after.

24
00:01:48,222 --> 00:01:56,451
For missing values compare variance retained across mean, median, K N N and regression imputation.

25
00:01:56,451 --> 00:02:05,603
For outliers compare mean, standard deviation and skew before and after, and a model score such as R squared.

26
00:02:05,603 --> 00:02:09,382
For encoding, justify one-hot versus ordinal.

27
00:02:09,382 --> 00:02:12,908
Do not just say that you cleaned the data:

28
00:02:12,908 --> 00:02:14,000
show numbers.

29
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:15,960
Avoid leakage.

30
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:24,573
Split the data before you fit scalers, imputers or resampling, and fit every step on training rows only.

31
00:02:24,573 --> 00:02:32,110
Remember that every treatment is a choice that changes results, so explain why you made it.

32
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:35,920
State the limitations of your cleaned dataset.

33
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:39,334
Here is a final checklist.

34
00:02:39,334 --> 00:02:40,842
Audit complete.

35
00:02:40,842 --> 00:02:43,556
Quality dimensions checked.

36
00:02:43,556 --> 00:02:45,467
Duplicates handled.

37
00:02:45,467 --> 00:02:50,795
Missing values explained and imputed with comparison.

38
00:02:50,795 --> 00:02:54,414
Outliers handled with a stated rule.

39
00:02:54,414 --> 00:02:58,536
Categories encoded and imbalance checked.

40
00:02:58,536 --> 00:03:00,145
Rules validated.

41
00:03:00,145 --> 00:03:03,362
Before and after evidence shown.

42
00:03:03,362 --> 00:03:06,177
A data quality log included.

43
00:03:06,177 --> 00:03:09,696
Good luck, and thanks for watching.

